# Pairs with EventualConvergence. Reproduces #2891 as a standing check: the
# last-writer-wins merge breaks an HLC tie on an observer-relative field, so
# every site ranks its own write lowest. a and b each write k1 at the same HLC
# and the two sites settle on different values for ever. It perturbs the merge
# definition, not an action.
MODULE: EventualConvergenceObserverRelativeTieBreak
TARGET: EventualConvergence
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: the LWW tie-break ranks the observer's own write lowest, so tied writes resolve differently per site (#2891)
BOUNDS: MaxFaults = 0, MaxHlc = 1

--- FIND
LwwRank(x, w) == Rank(w.o)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: an observer-relative tie-break.
LwwRank(x, w) == IF w.o = x THEN 0 ELSE Rank(w.o)
--- END
